105°C 378.15 0.03259 -25.77 $6.5 \times 10^{-12}$

Interpretation: The raw Arrhenius exponential is minuscule at all realistic junction temperatures. The observed thermal drift in the literature (on the order of $10^{-2}$ to $10^{-1}$ over months to years) arises from pre-exponential factors and field-enhanced migration effects not captured by the simple Arrhenius expression. The thermal drift term is operationally negligible below 60°C and becomes first-order only above 75–80°C.

Thermal regime classification:

