D.3 Endurance and Energy Budgets

Endurance budget. For a ten-year mission with an average recalibration interval of 4.7 hours, the total number of recalibrations is

N_{\text{cal}} = \frac{10 \times 365.25 \times 24}{4.7} \approx 18,650.

Each recalibration programs only cells whose conductance deviation exceeds the tolerance. The fraction of cells requiring reprogramming is estimated as

p_{\text{reprog}} \approx \frac{\Delta G_{\text{tol}}}{\sigma_{\text{drift}}} \approx 0.05.

The average number of writes per cell over the mission is

N_{\text{writes}} = N_{\text{cal}} \times p_{\text{reprog}} \approx 18,650 \times 0.05 = 933.

The worst-case cells (those with the highest drift) may require reprogramming at every recalibration:

N_{\text{writes,max}} = N_{\text{cal}} \approx 18,650.

The endurance limit for analog multi-level HfO₂ RRAM is approximately $1 \times 10^5$ writes. The safety margin is

\frac{1 \times 10^5}{18,650} \approx 5.4\times.

With wear-leveling (3× extension), the margin increases to approximately 16.1×.

Energy budget. The per-cell write energy for HfO₂ RRAM is approximately 5 pJ (typical for 100 ns write pulses at 2.5 V). The energy per recalibration is

E_{\text{cal}} = N_{\text{cells}} \times p_{\text{reprog}} \times E_{\text{write}}.

For Domain B with $N_{\text{cells}} = 8.4 \times 10^6$:

E_{\text{cal}} = 8.4 \times 10^6 \times 0.05 \times 5 \times 10^{-12} \text{ J} = 2.1 \text{ mJ}.

The average recalibration power is

P_{\text{cal}} = \frac{E_{\text{cal}}}{\tau_{\text{cal}}} = \frac{2.1 \times 10^{-3} \text{ J}}{4.7 \times 3600 \text{ s}} = 0.124 \text{ μW}.

This is negligible compared to the domain's 2.3 W power budget.

