E.3 Localized Hot-Spot Analysis

The thermal resistance values in Table E.2 are based on average die temperatures. In practice, localized hot spots within the RRAM crossbar tiles may exceed the average junction temperature by 20–40°C.

The hot-spot temperature rise is estimated using a simplified lateral heat spreading model:

\Delta T_{\text{hotspot}} = \frac{P_{\text{tile}}}{2\pi \kappa_{\text{Si}} t_{\text{die}}} \ln\left(\frac{r_{\text{spread}}}{r_{\text{tile}}}\right),

where $P_{\text{tile}}$ is the power dissipated in a single tile, $t_{\text{die}}$ is the die thickness, $r_{\text{tile}}$ is the tile radius, and $r_{\text{spread}}$ is the heat spreading radius.

