Packaging: Each die is packaged independently in a ceramic quad flat pack (CQFP) with 256 pins. System-level integration is achieved through PCB-level connections, not interposer assembly.

H.2 Built-In Self-Test (BIST) Infrastructure

· Boundary scan chains: IEEE 1149.1 JTAG interface for full crossbar conductance state readback and memory pattern writing.
· Ring oscillators: 64-stage ring oscillators in each domain for delay degradation tracking under TID exposure.
· PTAT thermal sensors: Proportional-to-absolute-temperature sensors with 0.5°C resolution, 64 per domain for thermal mapping.
· External sensor interface: Connector for commercial radiation monitor (RADMON, Liulin) input.

The on-die PIN diode array is retained as a research curiosity for SET pulse-width characterization, but is explicitly not the primary flux sensor.

H.3 Total Ionizing Dose Exposure Protocol

Facility: Cobalt-60 gamma source or 10 keV X-ray radiation tool.

Standard compliance: MIL-STD-883 Method 1019.9, ESCC Basic Specification No. 22900.

Dose rates:

· High Dose Rate (HDR): 50–300 rad(Si)/s
· Low Dose Rate (LDR): 0.01–0.1 rad(Si)/s (for ELDRS assessment)

Total dose targets:

· Domain A: 300 krad(Si)
· Domain B: 120 krad(Si) (maximum rated)
· Domain C: 200 krad(Si)
· Domain D: 120 krad(Si) (maximum rated)

Parameters monitored:

· RRAM conductance drift $\Delta G_{ij}(t)$
· Threshold voltage shifts $\Delta V_{\text{th}}$
· Subthreshold leakage $I_{\text{off}}$
· Ring oscillator frequency degradation
· Empirical thermal-radiation coupling coefficient $\kappa_{\text{emp}}$ at controlled temperatures (25°C, 50°C, 75°C, 100°C, 125°C)

H.4 Single-Event Effects Heavy-Ion Beam Test Protocol

Facility requirements:

· LET coverage: 1–85 MeV·cm²/mg
· Ion range in silicon: ≥ 30 μm
· Beam uniformity: > 90% over 30 mm × 30 mm area
· Flux control: 10²–10⁵ ions·cm⁻²·s⁻¹
· Environmental chamber: vacuum (P < 10⁻⁴ Torr), temperature control up to 125°C

Ion species:

Ion Energy (MeV) Surface LET (MeV·cm²/mg) Range in Si (μm)
²⁰Ne⁶⁺ 160 2.8 91.2
⁴⁰Ar¹¹⁺ 370 9.7 64.5
⁸⁴Kr²³⁺ 760 31.4 48.1
¹²⁹Xe³⁵⁺ 1140 58.8 41.3

Test angles: 0°, 30°, 45°, 60° (effective LET = LET₀/cos θ)

Weibull parameter extraction:

\sigma(\text{LET}_{\text{eff}}) = \begin{cases} 0, & \text{LET}_{\text{eff}} < \text{LET}_{\text{th}} \\ \sigma_{\text{sat}} \left[ 1 - \exp\left( -\left( \frac{\text{LET}_{\text{eff}} - \text{LET}_{\text{th}}}{W} \right)^S \right) \right], & \text{LET}_{\text{eff}} \ge \text{LET}_{\text{th}} \end{cases}

Parameters $\sigma_{\text{sat}}$, $\text{LET}_{\text{th}}$, $W$, and $S$ are extracted via Maximum Likelihood Estimation.

