H.6 Closed-Loop Model Calibration

Empirical parameter updates:

1. Measured SEU cross-sections update the fault injection layer
2. Measured $\kappa_{\text{emp}}$ updates the drift model and validates the thermal regime classification
3. Measured gating latency updates the CTMC transition rates
4. Empirical FORTRESS occupancy validates the Monte Carlo simulation approach and provides a benchmark for future analytical bounds

Calibrated reliability prediction:

\bar{\pi}_{\text{FORTRESS,cal}}^* \le \frac{\bar\lambda_{\text{SEP}} + \varepsilon_{\text{pred,emp}}\,\bar\lambda_{\text{false}}}{\bar\lambda_{\text{SEP}} + \varepsilon_{\text{pred,emp}}\,\bar\lambda_{\text{false}} + \mu_{F,\text{emp}}\,(1 - \delta_{\text{SEFI}})},

where $\delta_{\text{SEFI}}$ is the probability that a SEFI corrupts the recovery state machine before the gating command settles.

